| ''ni neiŋ'' || ''li laŋ'' || ''lin'' ({{zh-l|*恁}}) || ''tyøŋ'' ({{zh-l|*長}})
|-
! {{zh-l|*伊儂}} !! they
| ''i neiŋ'' || ''i laŋ'' || ''in'' ({{zh-l|*𪜶}}) || ''yøŋ'' ({{zh-l|*𪜶}})
|}
: A similar chain of changes happened in the Wu varieties to arrive at the modern divergent dialectal forms for “you (''singular'')”.
