==Chinese==

===Glyph origin===
{{Han etyl}}
In oracle bone script, it was likely a {{liushu|psc|nocap=yes}}: semantic {{zh-l|*凡}} + phonetic inverted {{och-l|由}}, hence a form vaguely similar to [[甲]]. It's also possible that the phonetic component is instead an ancient form of {{och-l|鏃}}.

In bronze inscriptions, {{zh-l|*凡}} corrupted into {{zh-l|*舟}}, and the bottom-right subcomponent of 甲 gradually corrupted into two lines [[巜]] (now written {{zh-l|*刂}}). The upper-right subcomponent (vaguely similar to 口) was eventually stylized as ({{zh-l|*亼}}) and moved to the top of the character in bamboo slips. Eventually, {{zh-l|*舟}} was further corrupted into {{zh-l|*月}}, arriving at the modern form [[俞]].

Unrelated to [[前]], [[刖]], [[巜]], and [[巛]].

