===Glyph origin===
From the removal of the two inner strokes from {{zh-l|*有|to have}}.

Attested at least since 1672, in {{lang|zh|《星餘筆記》}} by {{lw|zh|王鉞 (順治進士)|王鉞}}:
{{zh-x|寧 俗 樸鄙 所 陳 牒訴 多 用 土俗 書，初見 駭愕，習閒 亦 各 有 義意，令 略記 數字：……冇，音 茂，謂 無有 也。|When filing pleas, peasants in the Ning county ({{lang|zh|西寧縣}}, modern {{lang|zh|[[w:Yunan County|鬱南縣]]}}) often use the local popular writing, it is peculiar when first seen, but when accustomed, each has its meaning, for example: [...] {{lang|zh|冇}}, sounds like {{zh-m|*茂}}, means "to not have".|CL|ref=清・王鉞《星餘筆記》|collapsed=y}}

===Etymology 1===
{{zh-forms|alt=無,冒-Xiang}}
